    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="order" class="doc-h2">3. Wave order (do not skip ahead)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Each wave is a <strong>sub-project</strong>. Coordinator todos below point at owning-plan record_ids. Work those ids; do not clone the work here.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Wave</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Why this next</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Gate</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>W0</strong> Hermes + context</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Agents without settings and a worktree <code>.hermes.md</code> ignore Comserv rules (this session started that way).</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>.hermes.md</code> exists; aliases <code>code</code>/<code>cheap</code>/<code>local</code>/<code>delegate</code> resolve; default coding model unchanged.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>W1</strong> Right model on the right page</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Users still see an unfocused catalog. AIMPS P3/P2/P4 are the in-app equivalent of Hermes aliases.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">#2026–2029, #2036, then #2024/#2025, then #2030 done on their AIMPS projects.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>W2</strong> Agent runtime ready</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">AGENTS has projects and no todos. Notifications are email-only. Fine-tune leftovers compete with Router work.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">#268–270 have real todos; notification regression has a todo; stale AIC/OFT parked at P9.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>W3</strong> Operational agents</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Email agent then Secretary. In-app HelpDesk/Beekeeping/Ency stay blocked until their domain todos exist.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Mail feeds DailyPlan/error-audit; Secretary can call via VoIP page. Not started before W2 gate.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="chat-todo-agent" class="doc-h2">3b. In-chat Todo-create job (code now; runner later)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is <strong>code</strong> in <code>Model::AI2::TodoCreate</code>, called at the start of <code>AI2::Chat::process</code>. It is not a spawned LLM agent and it does not skip AISYSTEM W2 (the AGENTS runner). Chat-with-AI is the first caller; other agents should call the same Perl job later.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Tracking: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2217" class="doc-link" title="Opens todo #2217 — the work item that tracks this Todo-create agent (write a todo from chat, not navigate to a form).">todo #2217</a> on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=280" class="doc-link" title="Opens project #280 AISYSTEM, the project todo #2217 is attached to.">#280 AISYSTEM</a>.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Step (agent settings)</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Job</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Parse</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Read intent. Ask only for missing subject or project. Infer priority/due/scheduled_date (queue eligibility). Do NOT invent blockers or a queue-aware start_date here — that is the Scheduler agent (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Opens todo #2218: Scheduler agent for blockers and start dates that respect the existing queue.">#2218</a>). LOOKUP/READ_DOCS may refine later.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">LOOKUP_TODOS (sub-agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Similar open todos on this SiteName — do not duplicate.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">LOOKUP_PROJECTS (sub-agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Match project/sub-project on current SiteName. If none, ask to create a project.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">READ_DOCS (sub-agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Skim /Documentation for the topic so the todo is grounded in what the app already has.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">WRITE</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Create the row in code (TodoCreate), not by asking the chat model to invent a form. If the request is unclear, a cheap already-warm model may extract subject/project JSON only.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> user says “add/create a todo …” in the widget, <code>/ai/widget</code>, or the editor chat.</li>
                <li><strong>Model:</strong> none for a clear “add a todo …” (fastest, $0 — no LLM). The dropdown model must not own the write. If phrasing is unclear, extract subject/project with a <em>free already-warm</em> OpenRouter model (Nemotron nano is fine for that — no Ollama cold load). Use local Ollama only if it is already resident. The model returns JSON; <code>TodoCreate</code> writes the row. Nemotron’s failure was inventing a fake Add box, not being too dumb to parse a title.</li>
                <li><strong>Job:</strong> SiteName of the current site → match project/sub-project → ask to create a project if none fit → write a todo with <code>project_id</code>, <code>scheduled_date</code> (today), developer = logged-in user, so it shows in planning.</li>
                <li><strong>Code:</strong> <code>Model::AI2::TodoCreate</code> + intercept at the start of <code>AI2::Chat::process</code> (the path <code>/ai2/chat</code> always takes). Shared JS: <code>ai-chat/feature-todo.js</code>.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Built (2026-08-20):</strong> clear “add a todo …” never reaches the picker model. Parse infers scheduled_date / NEW / priority / due; asks only if subject is vague or no project matches; WRITE uses current SiteName. <code>/ai/widget</code> loads <code>feature-todo.js</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Not built:</strong> LOOKUP_TODOS / READ_DOCS as separate callable agents; Nemotron-JSON extract for messy phrasing; other agents calling this job via the W2 runner; blockers and queue-aware start_date (that is <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Scheduler agent tracking todo.">#2218</a>).</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="scheduler-agent" class="doc-h2">3c. Scheduler agent (specified — not built)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is <strong>not</strong> Parse and not bulk Reschedule. Tracking: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Opens todo #2218 on project #280 — Scheduler agent that creates predecessor blocker todos and sets start_date after the current queue, without rewriting every todo.">todo #2218</a> on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=280" class="doc-link" title="Project #280 AISYSTEM, the project this scheduler work is attached to.">#280 AISYSTEM</a>.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Today, creating a todo does <em>not</em> create its blockers. If the work cannot start until an inventory item exists, that inventory-create work should be a <strong>blocking predecessor</strong> (<code>is_blocking</code> / <code>blocked_by_todo_id</code>). Start dates also ignore the queue: if open work may take a month, the new todo should not start today. The old <code>/todo/reschedule</code> path rewrote <code>start_date</code>/<code>time_of_day</code> on every row and produced noise — do not revive that.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Job:</strong> one agent that only makes schedule order: propose (then write, after compare) blocker chains and capacity-aware start dates.</li>
                <li><strong>Callers:</strong> Todo-create after WRITE; Daily Plan; later the AGENTS runner. Cross-plan: scoring lives in planning (#138 / TodoRanking); this agent uses it, does not replace it.</li>
                <li><strong>Safety:</strong> advisory preview first (same lesson as FocusTune weights). Never bulk-mutate the queue.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="chat-invoice" class="doc-h2">3d. Invoice from chat (draft only — shipped 2026-08-26)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Code in <code>Model::AI2::InvoiceCreate</code>, same intercept as TodoCreate. Tracking: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2311" class="doc-link">#2311</a> on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=121" class="doc-link">#121 AIC-004</a>. Reuses existing Inventory tables — no new schema. Chat never Posts the GL.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> “enter/record this invoice from &lt;supplier&gt; for $X …” or “create a sales invoice for &lt;name&gt; for $X”.</li>
                <li><strong>Write:</strong> supplier bill → draft on <code>inventory_supplier_invoices</code> (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/invoice') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/invoice</a>). Sales → draft on <code>inventory_customer_invoices</code> (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/sales') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/sales</a>). SiteName of the page. Admin or accounting role. Missing amount or unknown supplier: ask.</li>
                <li><strong>Not built:</strong> auto-create supplier; Post GL from chat; line-item SKU matching.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="shipped-0826" class="doc-h2">3e. Shipped 2026-08-26 (aisystem worktree — not committed)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Branch <code>aisystem</code>. Do not treat schema-branch table creation as in scope. User reviews diffs before commit.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Item</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Tracking</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Code / gate</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">SuperGrok first; never OpenRouter Grok</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2313" class="doc-link">#2313</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>Router::_detect_provider</code> remaps <code>grok-*</code> and <code>openrouter|x-ai/grok-*</code> to SuperGrok. Default is SuperGrok <code>grok-4.6</code> when OAuth exists. Fail → OpenRouter <code>:free</code> (no grok slug) then Ollama. Tests in <code>t/model_ai2_router_outage.t</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">OpenRouter 503 retry + clean errors</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2292" class="doc-link">#2292</a> / <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2293" class="doc-link">#2293</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">502/503/504 retry twice (1s, 2s) then hop-down. Widget never shows raw <code>OpenRouter provider error: 503</code>. Fallback keeps the same system prompt / ACTION contract.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Invoice from chat</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2311" class="doc-link">#2311</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>InvoiceCreate</code> + <code>/ai2/action create_invoice</code>. Draft only. <code>t/model_ai2_invoice_create.t</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Positive learning (partial)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=288" class="doc-link">#288 AILEARN</a> <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2299" class="doc-link">#2299</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>KnowledgeRecall</code> injects prior docs/todos into the system prompt with UNVERIFIED/INTERNAL labels. It currently reads the DB <code>documentation</code> table, which is empty — live KB is file-based <code>root/Documentation</code>. Next: point recall at the file store. No new table on this branch (schema later).</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-warning">Next AISYSTEM-specified work after this: Scheduler <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link">#2218</a>, or W1 AIMPS shortlists <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2194" class="doc-link">#2194</a>. Do not start schema <code>AiKnowledge</code> from aisystem.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hermes" class="doc-h2">4. Hermes focus settings (W0 — applied 2026-08-19)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Settings live in <code>~/.hermes/config.yaml</code> via <code>hermes config set</code> (never hand-edit). Secrets stay in <code>~/.hermes/.env</code>.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Role</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Alias</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Resolved</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">When</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Coding (this agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>code</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>xai-oauth/grok-4.6</code> (also the session default)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Comserv edits, plans, audits</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Cheap / local / delegate</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>cheap</code> <code>local</code> <code>delegate</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Ollama <code>qwen2.5-coder:14b</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Subagents, triage, summaries. <code>delegation.model</code> already this.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">Also on this machine (not aliased): <code>qwen2.5:72b</code>, <code>gemma4-64k</code>, <code>phi4:14b</code>. Use 72b only when a local deep-read beats a paid call. In-session: <code>/model code</code> or <code>/model cheap</code>.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Remaining worktree <code>.hermes.md</code> files are owned by <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2142" class="doc-link">todo #2142</a> on GITWT-NEW — raised, not absorbed.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="providers" class="doc-h2">4b. In-app providers (current)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The /ai and /ai2 model dropdown (and the floating Chat with AI widget) has <strong>four groups</strong>. SuperGrok is not a nickname for xAI.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Group</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Wire prefix</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Who sees it</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Credential (any container)</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Ollama (Local)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>ollama|…</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">All roles (local models)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Live Ollama on the host</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">SuperGrok (prepaid)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>supergrok|grok-4.6</code> first</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">admin / developer / editor only</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>/run/secrets/supergrok_oauth</code>, mounted <code>/home/comserv/.comserv/secrets/supergrok_oauth</code>, env <code>SUPERGROK_OAUTH_TOKEN</code>, or Ency <code>UserApiKeys</code> service <code>supergrok</code>. Sync from Hermes: <code>perl script/sync_supergrok_token.pl</code>. Host <code>~/.hermes/auth.json</code> is last-resort workstation-only.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">xAI (Grok)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>grok|…</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">admin / developer / editor only</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Pay-per-token <code>GROK_API_KEY</code> / <code>/run/secrets/grok_api_key</code> / DB service <code>grok</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">OpenRouter</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>openrouter|…</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Role-filtered (guests: :free only)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OpenRouter key (k8s / env / DB)</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-warning">The same slug <code>grok-4.6</code> can appear under SuperGrok and under xAI. Pick SuperGrok (prepaid) to spend weekly credits. Router (2026-08-26): <code>grok-*</code> and <code>openrouter|x-ai/grok-*</code> are remapped to SuperGrok. App default is SuperGrok <code>grok-4.6</code> when the OAuth token exists — not paid OpenRouter. SuperGrok fail → cheaper OpenRouter <code>:free</code> (never a Grok slug) → Ollama. After send, status must stay SuperGrok if SuperGrok answered; if it fell back, the :free/Ollama hop is correct, not Grok-on-OpenRouter.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">W1.0 (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2202" class="doc-link">#2202</a>) delivered the four-group picker. Routing fix <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2313" class="doc-link">#2313</a>. Remaining W1 is AIMPS shortlists/sort, not another provider.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="park" class="doc-h2">5. Parked until W1 gate (do not cancel)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">These stay in the DB at priority 9 so they stop winning the daily queue:</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>AIC leftover phases #242–246 (AIC-007..011) — predates Router/AIMPS</li>
                <li>Ollama fine-tune / Modelfile OFT #266–278</li>
                <li>chain_query multi-model #262–265 — after shortlists exist</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Keep live: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=562" class="doc-link" title="Older live todo: AI create todos.">#562</a>, <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2217" class="doc-link" title="Todo-create job (code).">#2217</a>, <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Scheduler agent (specified).">#2218</a>, #778 (document adding a project), GITWT Hermes context #2142–2146, AIMPS #2024–2036.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="project-tracking" class="doc-h2">6. Project Tracking</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Owning project:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=280" class="doc-link">#280 (AISYSTEM)</a>
                — parent:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=114" class="doc-link">#114 AIC-ENH</a>
                — grandparent:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=63" class="doc-link">#63 AiIntegration</a>.
                Todos:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo') %]?project_id=280" class="doc-link">under #280</a>.
                Each wave is a sub-project.
            </p>
